{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/935672-children-of-the-corn","id":935672,"title":"Children of the Corn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-22T10:27:59-07:00","id":935672,"title":"Children of the Corn","content":"As you would adapt the movie / book? Would some supernatural feature children as in the book? And how to adapt corrupt children of Little Fears? And what would be the entedida they follow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T17:48:50-07:00","id":935878,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Children of the Corn </b><br /> <br /> Hmm - its been forever since I have read the story or seen the movie, but from my memory the &quot;Children&quot; operate like a Mystery Cult with a particularly nasty ephemeral (either a Spirit of the Harvest, or some type of G_M Angel) as their patron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T18:17:54-07:00","id":935883,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> I was looking at some alternatives, an idigam or the Pangaean Harvest, but they would all be way too powerful for the level of power seen in the Children of the Corn. One small farm town can be controlled like that by a Rank 4 or 5 spirit or other ephemeral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:46:46-07:00","id":935948,"title":"","content":"You'd also want to look at Innocents: I'm pretty sure that has information on how to run horror with child characters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T07:04:42-07:00","id":936070,"title":"","content":"I just re-read the original story from Stephen King's <i>Night Shift</i>. Here are some observations<br /> <br /> The Children of the Corn are definitely a Mystery Cult, following a bizarre version of Christianity that is mostly Old Testament fire and brimstone blended with the worship of a figure called &quot;He Who Walks Behind the Rows&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;He Who Walks Behind the Rows&quot; is presented as a entity seen only by its enormous presence and burning red eyes. In CofD terms, he seems to be a harvest spirit that has gained some influence over the hearts and minds of the youth in the township, compelling his flock to sacrifice anyone over the age of 19. While it would be easy to run the spirit has rank 4 or 5 , for a game with mostly Mortals, a Rank 3 spirit would still be strong enough to achieve this level of influence. <hr /><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mystery Cult - Children of the Corn</span></b><br /> Initiation Benefits</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u25cf - Even the youngest among the Children can quote scripture readily. They gain an Occult specialty in &quot;Biblical Scripture&quot;<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - The Children learn to navigate the seemingly endless acres of corn with ease. They gain the Direction Sense Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - The Children must be prepared to do violence in the name of &quot;He Who Walks Behind the Rows&quot;. They gain a dot of Weaponry.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Some among the Children see the signs and hear the voice of &quot;He Who Walks Behind the Rows&quot;. They gain Omen Sensitivity Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - There are Leaders among the Children, who direct the flock and enforce the will of &quot;He Who Walks Behind the Rows&quot;. They gain the Inspiring Merit.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>He Who Walks Behind the Rows</b></span><br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 6, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 16, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 18<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Plants 2, Faith 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on a person over 19 years old; <b>Bane:</b> Burning Corn<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Awe, Implant Mission, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Seek</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  Updated 07-23-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T12:09:10-07:00","id":936183,"title":"","content":"I find the bane fitting: it explains why HWWB wants all adults killed, because he cannot controls them ( albeit with those attributes is pretty much a walking mixer of PCs who don't figure out his bane quickly ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:00:59-07:00","id":936228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/935672-children-of-the-corn?p=936183#post936183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the bane fitting</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be spelled otherwise though:<br /> <br /> Burning corn.<br /> <br /> Banes are materials or substances, not accidents or some specific scenario that harms the thing. Those would be Bans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}